C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\xscaleinten\fable_adjudication_20260912.md:9:**VERDICT: D1 is clause (e) for both cells (the cost-graded lean is OVERTURNED; the rows stay as L1). Codex's three predicted gaps are all coverage debt, none a floor breach; the repair chain CLOSES on this pass (zero floor breaches, enumeration below). F11's shrink channel is a named, filed measurement. Wrong-as-recorded: the D1 lean, and F15's rationale (the fix made the `sh ?` guard load-bearing, which nobody said). xscale is commit-ready behind a green gate plus a CHANGELOG grade; PPC is commit-ready once the parked gate section is restored with its pins verified, the F15 record is rewritten, and the stray `ppc_rldicl_probe.py` edit is scoped in or out by name.** Evidence basis: 7/7 scriptable seats plus the Opus measuring seat; agy deliberately not fired (measurement reservation). I read the tree, both tables, all three CONTRACTs and `cpu_arm_coproc.c:304-333`; I built nothing.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\xscaleinten\fable_adjudication_20260912.md:11:**Q1 — D1: clause (e), both cells.** Rule text: *"A value or combination the body never tests as a case (`idata == k`; a byte no conditional distinguishes...) is DISCLOSED under clause (e)"*, and the pass-11 bound: *"the FLOOR ... is the cross-product of the guard's dominating predicates with the device-STATE lvalues the fix's own repair path reads."* The dominating predicates are `crm==0`, `crn==0`, `l_bit`; the body (`:311`) reads `rd` as an index and `i80321_inten` as a source and tests neither, so the floor is the accept cell alone — already pinned by the value rows. Three seats (kimi CLI, ollama-kimi, glm) hold `rd == 0` as floor by the operand-swap clause: substitute the body-read `rd` into the dominating `crn == 0`, inheriting its constant. I rule against that majority-of-three on three grounds: the swap clause binds itself to *"the guard-field/body-field grep"*, which is about STATE fields that can disagree at different write sites, not instruction-encoding operands; the pass-11 bound names device-STATE lvalues, and `rd` is not one; and the swap reading makes floor membership depend on which constant the sibling dispatch happened to carry (`rd==0` only because `crn==0` dominates — had the arm been `crn 4`, `rd==4` would be floor and `rd==0` not). Grading by coincidence is the same vice as grading by cost. Codex's withdrawal is right. **Rule for the next pure deletion whose guarded body tests nothing: the floor is clause (b) verbatim reinstatement plus the dominating predicates' accept cell; every re-introduction keyed on a body-read operand the body does not test (`rd == k`, `field & bit`, `field == v`) is clause (e), disclosed BY CLASS in the CONTRACT; any row added for one is L1 construction — licensed because cheap, never graded floor because cheap.** Grade F1/F2 as L1 + (e) in the CHANGELOG. Two corrections to seat claims: glm's "bit 28 is driven, so F2's record is false" misreads the packet — bit 28 is listed as a DRIVEN value and bit 22 as the key, which is correct; codex's F2 refinement stands (all-ones pins every single-bit-SET predicate, not bit-clear or multi-bit patterns — say so).
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\xscaleinten\fable_adjudication_20260912.md:13:**Q2 — codex's three gaps: debt, not breach; the chain closes.** (a) `n = sh & ~7`: the rotate loop's only tested partition is `n != 0` ({0, >0}), rowed at SH=0 and SH>0; dropping low bits of the count is a value-domain edit the body never tests as a case → (e). (b) wrap-only re-read: the mask loop has no wrap test (wrapping is implicit in `& 63`), so wrap/non-wrap is not a body-tested partition → (e); same shape as F10's residual, and codex itself says it justifies no floor demand. (c) Rc-conditioned skip: `rc` is tested in the enclosing function but neither dominates the edited lines nor is read by either edited loop's body, so under the letter of DEPENDS-ON (*"predicates DOMINATING the edited lines ... swaps drawn ONLY from fields the guarded BODY reads"*) it is outside the enumeration → (e); it is the strongest of the three because the record-form rows purported to cover it, and both CONTRACTs now disclose it, which discharges the record. **The cap:** *"THE CAP COUNTS ASKS, NEVER FINDINGS"* — pass 2 was the one ask-again; this §F2 pass is mandated, not an ask, and *"everything ONE ask returns is disposed of INDIVIDUALLY under L1–L4 and the floor."* So the cap forbids nothing here, and L1 (*"the row is part of the deliverable still being built"*) licenses any of these rows. **The repair-chain rule decides whether they are OWED: it closes on the first VALID pass with zero floor breaches carried with its denominator.** Denominator: M_RD0, M_MAGICBIT, D_SKIP_FULL_ROT, D_ALIAS_REREAD measured killed; RM_GE, DM_NOAND_END measured killed; codex (a)/(b)/(c), F16, F5 enumerated as (e). Zero breaches → closed. **On `full rot` → SH=63, MB=1:** licensed as L1, and I verified the arithmetic (end `(64-63)&63 = 1 = MB`, full mask; ROTL64 = `0xEF56DF77E57F7806`, byte-rounded `0x0DDEADBEEFCAFEF0`); with SH=0 already rowed it closes the whole single-operator bit-masking class, not one cell — the repair-chain amendment's own preference. But do NOT modify the measured row: `full rot` at SH=24 is table 3's cited sole killer of D_SKIP_FULL_ROT and the POSTTABLE's "the shipped probe IS the instrument" claim rests on it. ADD a row, and know the cost: session 3 changes, D_NOCIRC's unmasked loop with `end = 1` will behave differently, so the D_ legs owe a table 4 with predictions written first, plus pin 29→30. Not owed before commit; the one row I would spend a ten-leg re-run on if the owner is willing; otherwise file it with this exact spec, folding F16 and (a) into one item.
