C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbctrlportkill_20260924\pass_v6\fable5_f2_v6.md:12:The rule as written has three bounds, and the floor reading drops all three. The floor is the guard's dominating predicates crossed with the device-state lvalues the repair path reads, where jointly reachable; "the bits of the single value being written are single-operand MARGINALS, not floor"; and the generating-set sentence adds, at each floor cell, "every idata bit the guarded body TESTS" — minted on `idata & ICLR`, a bit the body MASKS. This arm tests `writeflag`, `idata >= 8` and `!warned_port`. Its floor is {write} × {below, at, past 8} × {latch clear, set}: six cells, all held (A's accepts; 8 first-refused in P, W, B; 9, 0x100, 0x100000005, all-ones first-refused in F, V, X, Y; the set-latch cells by every later refusal). No bit is masked; #548 ruled that a relational compare's generating set is its three regions. Latch-clear × bit k is therefore a two-axis joint of a floor cell with a marginal — the class (0) already discloses in general terms.
