C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\opus_pass2_20260912\OPUS_REPORT.md:30:M_ALIGNDECLINE is the canonical (d) shape, `if (X)` -> `if (X && Y)`, applied to the dominating `writeflag != MEM_WRITE` arm. Its Y reads `d->dmaaddr`, which is the body-read field, so it falls inside the DEPENDS-ON bound as the brief states it. Under Fable's pass-1 rule, "value-keyed = clause (e)", you could argue it down to (e). But the contract does not disclose it as (e): the NOT COVERED list covers only value-keyed exits, not value-keyed declines. Either way the record is wrong, and the repair is cheap: one read-back row with an aligned value such as 0x0c0f0000, plus one session that writes ENABLE=1 first. Those two rows kill four of the survivors (both DECLINEs and both EXITs).
