C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\gdromexitsix\r2measure_20260829\RESULTS.md:119:## The floor clauses, measured rather than argued
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass2_20260912.md:16:**VERDICT: HOLD — the FIX stands unchanged (ACCEPT, no seat disputes it), the grades are UPHELD with two warrants replaced (D2's alias set is the eight-cell single-bit generating set of the selector, so `case 0x00` is FLOOR as codex argues; D1's alignment decline is an IN-BOUND value cell the body does not partition, NOT "outside the BOUND" as the shipped header now says), targeted table 4 is VALID on its superset warrant — but the repair chain does NOT close: two exact edits are predicted to sweep the 35-row instrument on the FLOOR channel, inside the contract's own claim: `fatal("GXemul> ");` (no newline: glued to the front of the next prompt line, which the grammar admits and the count counts once) and `fatal("GXemul> quit\n");` (the accounting's one exemption). That is the THIRD consecutive pass finding one class — a whitelist oracle with a legal shape or an exemption to hide in — so the next repair owes the CLASS CLOSURE (pre-quit snapshot, exact expected line content, zero exemptions), a targeted table 5, and gate 10 re-run on the repaired probe. Evidence basis: 7/7 scriptable seats on both passes, Opus measuring seat, four kill tables read against their mutators and raw logs; I built and ran nothing.**
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass2_20260912.md:22:**D1 — UPHOLD (e) / rows L1, and CORRECT THE REASON in the header.** Two different not-floor reasons were written as one. `} else if (d->dmaaddr & 0x1f)` keys on the body-read field — it is INSIDE DEPENDS-ON clause (2) — and is not floor because the body induces no partition of that field (joint-cells rule: *"a value or combination the body never tests as a case ... is DISCLOSED under clause (e)"*; the bounded form: *"the bits of the single value ... are single-operand MARGINALS, not floor"*). `!d->enable`, the static counter and `len` are OUTSIDE the enumeration (not body-read lvalues; `len` is the tail's argument). Opus's `if (X) -> if (X && Y)` shape argument is refuted by its own consequence: it makes `M_BIT30`, `M_EQ4` and `M_ZEROEXIT` floor too and kills the pass-1 and xscaleinten rules (grok). Grading by the consumer's tests is the transitive chasing the bound forbids. The shipped header's sentence *"the consumer-keyed forms (`enable`, the alignment bits, the read count) are outside the BOUND"* is an L4 wrong record on the alignment half — `d->dmaaddr` IS what the body reads. One-line fix.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass2_20260912.md:26:**F3 / F5 (glm, minimax: "extensions of (e), outside the BOUND") — REFINE, my fault.** Clause (e) is THE CONTRACT — the disclosure clause for everything not floor — not a category defined by "body-read operand". My pass-1 sentence named one (e) sub-class and read as a definition, and two seats read it that way. Both seats are right that `len` and the counter are outside the BOUND; that IS the reason they are (e)-disclosed, not an alternative to it. CHANGELOG form: *"(e); not floor because outside the DEPENDS-ON enumeration (len / the counter / enable are not body-read lvalues)"* versus *"(e); not floor because a value cell of the body-read field, which the body does not partition (alignment, == 4, == 0, bit 30)"*. Note minimax's companion survivor ("the write arm is uncovered") is false on the packet — every value row is store-then-load — so count its argument, not the seat.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass2_20260912.md:34:**Denominator swept (all measured unless marked):** (b) reinstatement whole and by half (HEAD, KEEPFATAL, EXITONLY); selector P1: hoist, `& 4` redirect, six of eight single-bit narrowings (`& ~0x10`, `& ~0x04` unmeasured, predicted kills); P2 `writeflag`: two-valued, no cell (EQUIVALENT, disclosed); body-read field value cells: EQ4, BIT30, ZEROEXIT, MASKLOW, ALIGN/EN decline and exit, JOINTDECLINE; tail: RET0, LEN, LEN1, odata placement (EQUIVALENT); side effects: READCLEAR, SIBLING; counter: THIRDREAD; diagnostics: verbatim, reworded, latched, token-free, hex, blank, CR, prompt-line. Thirty-three mutants plus HEAD across four tables, plus Opus's seven. Clause (c) was never a leg — the four control rows carry it by construction; name the measurement (a binary without the maple device at 0x5f6c00 must red `ctrl devsig maple`) rather than assert it.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass2_20260912.md:49:2. **The header's "alignment bits ... outside the BOUND"** — L4; the operand is body-read.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\mapledmaaddr\fable_pass1_20260912.md:13:**Q2 — row list, under my xscaleinten Q1 rule** (*"the floor is clause (b) verbatim reinstatement plus the dominating predicates' accept cell; every re-introduction keyed on a body-read operand the body does not test (`rd == k`, `field & bit`, `field == v`) is clause (e), disclosed BY CLASS; any row added for one is L1 — licensed because cheap, never graded floor because cheap"*). The body `odata = d->dmaaddr;` tests nothing; dominating predicates `relative_addr == 0x04`, `writeflag != MEM_WRITE`.
