C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbd5\fable_adj_20260923\FABLE_ADJ_ANSWER_20260923.md:40:Predicted scores: 333/333 and 37/37 for each. This is the #499 shape: X4 closed "a +0x18c guard conditioned on irq_enable" on the READ guard and left the same conjunct on the direction predicate open at every arm. The reset state is jointly reachable through the device's own data flow (the memset), so it is a floor cell, L2. **Rows owed:** offline, a fresh all-zero instance with NO prior decline -- each legal read (four status registers plus +0x188, widths 1/2/4: announce 0, value 0) and each enable write (Set/Clear x IRQ/FIQ x 0/0x70: announce 0, enable as expected), then decline all five and require exactly 5 announces (the latches were still clear). Guest (recommended): reads of +0x180/+0x184/+0x280/+0x284 at the head of arm S before the enable stores, scored on a buffer MARK -- `fatals` is a whole-buffer regex (`footbridge_sites_probe.py:419`), so "no footbridge line before the first decline step" is the row that attributes, and it also discharges G18 for that segment. If the build refutes me (say X7's order is not what I read), the verdict is CLOSE with the Q4 corrections.
