C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\wdc473floor\pass1_20261009\fable5_pass1.md:68:Opus's objection is right about the ENUMERATION and wrong about what it bounds.  DEPENDS-ON bounds which CELLS a row is owed for (dominating predicates x jointly reachable state); it was adopted against transitive data-flow chasing.  P1 demands no new cell -- it strengthens the ORACLE at a cell the shipped row already holds (200000 / 131072).  A row that checks 1 of the 32768 bytes the repair delivers observes 1/32768 of the repair's effect; that is the anchor-rule shape ("anchored" at index 0 only) and the CHANNEL line, not a new enumeration axis.  And the class is diff-closed: the diff carries exactly two index expressions, and a whole-chunk compare at each site kills every single-site edit of that expression at once -- no chain.  Two findings of one class across two passes (`Md_wrongoff`, `Md_frozenj`) also trigger the class-closure amendment: close every cell in one diff, which is what P1 + whole-chunk P2 do.
