C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\assertrow_review_20261009\FALLBACK_opus48_ruling_v1_20261009.md:16:* `assert` is the REPAIR'S OWN WRITE TARGET, and the enclosing function distinguishes it at `if (assert)` (:399), three lines below the repair. Per the JOINT-CELLS clause (2026-09-04) the floor enumerates {guard operand} x {body-read lvalue the body distinguishes}; the partition `if (assert)` induces is {0,nonzero}. Per the derived-input clause (7n-5, 2026-10-09) a local feeding a body-read operand gets the partition the body induces on IT. So the 2x2 is {C040 clear,set} x {assert 0,1}.
