C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\assertrow_review_20261009\FALLBACK_opus48_ruling_v1_20261009.md:22:BOUND. One cell, one row. The enumeration is the diff-closed 2x2; three cells are rowed; (set,0) is the fourth. Closing it is the class-closure the repair-chain rule wants in ONE diff. It does not recurse and cannot grow: {C040} x {assert 0,1} is the whole product the body distinguishes.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\assertrow_review_20261009\FALLBACK_opus48_ruling_v1_20261009.md:30:DISPOSITION. L2. The round is closed, so "in-round" becomes a FOLLOW-UP COMMIT (late-dissent rule: MEASURED FALSE PASS against the floor -> L2 in a follow-up). The commit is REGRESS-ONLY (one row in `pcc2_c040_probe.py`, gate count 18->19 in `gate_arm.sh`); the fix is correct and dev_pcc2.c is NOT touched. That follow-up owes its own pass 2 (repair-chain), scoped to the one-row diff, closing on the first pass with zero breaches.
